  "A photo has a regular, repeating diagonal pattern of lines caused by an electrical interference. The photographer wants to remove this periodic noise without affecting the rest of the image’s details. Which filtering approach is the most effective for this situation?\nA. Using a correlation filter, because it is more computationally efficient than a convolution filter for this type of problem.\nB. Using a kernel-based spatial filter (convolution filter), because it can directly target and average out the noisy pixels.\nC. Using a Fourier transform-based filter, because it allows the noise to be isolated and removed directly from the frequency domain.\nD. Adjusting the image histogram, because this can improve the contrast and make the noise less noticeable.\nC",
